 ```
 
+A sixth subkey, `eventsGroup`, controls the summarizing events group card shown for a run of tool/event messages. It accepts one of three modes (`none` is not a valid value here, since a fully collapsed card is already the default `live` outcome once work finishes):
+
+- `live` (default): the most recent events group stays open while its session is active, and collapses once work finishes. This reproduces the pre-existing behavior.
+- `last`: the most recent events group stays open regardless of session activity.
+- `all`: every events group in the transcript stays open. On a long session history this renders substantially more DOM, since a group's body is only rendered while open.
+
+The `live` class and `live events` label are shown only for the most recent group of an active session, independent of the chosen mode. Manual collapsing/expanding is remembered per group in any mode. Because this release also changes the storage key events groups use to persist their disclosure state, every previously saved group disclosure choice resets once after upgrading.
+
